      ],
      "source": "https://thebostondaybook.com/historical-places-in-huntington/",
      "category": "nature",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The town’s name honors Charles Huntington, who donated $100 to establish its first library.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        18
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Huntington%2C_Massachusetts",
      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "In 1841 the Western Railroad reached Huntington, spurring manufacturing and drawing new settlers to the area.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        3
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Huntington%2C_Massachusetts",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Stanton Hall, a historic landmark in Huntington, remains a symbol of the town’s early architectural heritage.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
